  "documentation": {
	"summary": "This randomness hall restores four existing works before Random_Game.",
	"layout": "15 by 25 cells. Pollock anchors the front; Monte Carlo sits left of the middle route, pipes to the right, and the particle study occupies the rear-left bay. Both sides of the floor painting and the right rear aisle remain open.",
	"objective": "Ask what each random choice is permitted to change, and which rules continue to decide the result.",
	"key_elements": [
	  "pollock_painting_in_3d at column 7, row 6: full-scale floor support, 4.34 by 2.94 m including its frame.",
	  "monte_carlo_dartboard at column 4, row 12: faces the entry; separate compact controls sit 1.0 m in front.",
	  "pipe_dream at column 10, row 15: quarter-scale bounded growth, lifted 1.15 m; its centreline occupies at most 3 by 2 by 3 m.",
	  "extreme_randomness at column 5, row 20: all five chapters cycle at scale 0.2, lifted 1.5 m.",
      "Spawn at column 7, row 0; the rear teleporter at column 7, row 24 continues to Random_Game in the randomness museum."
	]
  },
